---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PrivacyBadge from '../../components/PrivacyBadge.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Compress Image Locally — JPG, PNG & WebP | ZeroSend" description="Compress JPG, PNG, or WebP images directly in your browser. Adjust quality and download the result without uploading the selected image for processing.">
  <JsonLd data={{ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication', name:'ZeroSend Image Compressor', applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication', operatingSystem:'Any modern web browser', isAccessibleForFree:true }} />
  <section class="tool-page"><div class="container narrow-wide">
    <p class="eyebrow">IMAGE TOOL</p><h1>Image Compressor</h1><p class="lead">Reduce an image's file size locally. Compare the original and result before downloading.</p><PrivacyBadge />
    <div class="tool-shell" data-image-compressor>
      <label class="dropzone"><strong>Choose an image</strong><span>JPG, PNG or WebP</span><input type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" /></label>
      <div class="controls hidden" data-controls>
        <label>Output format<select data-format><option value="same">Same as input</option><option value="image/jpeg">JPG</option><option value="image/webp">WebP</option><option value="image/png">PNG</option></select></label>
        <label>Quality <output data-quality-output>80%</output><input data-quality type="range" min="10" max="100" value="80" /></label>
        <button class="button primary" data-process type="button">Compress image</button>
      </div>
      <p class="status" data-status id="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
      <div class="result hidden" data-result><img data-preview alt="Preview of compressed image" /><div class="stats"><div><span>Original</span><strong data-original-size></strong></div><div><span>Result</span><strong data-result-size></strong></div><div><span>Change</span><strong data-saving></strong></div></div><a class="button primary" data-download download>Download compressed image</a></div>
    </div>
    <article class="content-block"><h2>How to compress an image without uploading it</h2><ol><li>Select a JPG, PNG, or WebP file.</li><li>Choose an output format and quality.</li><li>Compress and inspect the result size.</li><li>Download the locally generated image.</li></ol><h2>What changes image size?</h2><p>Lossy JPG and WebP can trade visual detail for smaller files. PNG uses lossless compression, so the quality slider does not meaningfully reduce a PNG unless you convert it to a lossy format.</p><h2>Common uses</h2><p>Compress website photos, email attachments, presentation images, and social assets before sending or publishing them.</p><h2>Limits and browser support</h2><p>JPG, PNG and WebP inputs are limited to 25 MiB, 8192 pixels per side and 16 megapixels total. The WebP converter accepts JPG and PNG only. A smaller image may be needed on phones with limited memory. Unsupported encoders report an error. Animated images become a single still frame; metadata and color profiles may change. Transparent pixels become white when exporting JPG.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is my image uploaded?</h3><p>No. The selected image is decoded and re-encoded in your browser for this tool.</p><h3>Will compression always make the file smaller?</h3><p>No. Already-optimized files, small images, or conversion to a less efficient setting can stay similar in size or grow.</p><h2>Related tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/jpg-png-to-webp">JPG / PNG to WebP</a> · <a href="/tools/image-resizer">Image Resizer</a></p></article>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { initImageTool } from '../../scripts/image-tool';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-image-compressor]');
  if (root) initImageTool(root, 'compress');
</script>
